@startuml SillycationEpisodeStateDiagram
title Sillycation - Episode State Diagram

hide empty description

'Initial State
[*] --> DRAFT : Episode created

'Episode State

state DRAFT
state SUBMITTED
state VOTING
state COMPLETED

'Transition
DRAFT --> SUBMITTED : submit()\n[author requests submission\nand Trip is ACTIVE]

SUBMITTED --> VOTING : openVoting()\n[automatic after successful submission]

VOTING --> COMPLETED : complete()\n[all eligible participants have voted]

COMPLETED --> [*]

'State Rules
note right of DRAFT
  The Episode is editable.

  Only the author may edit
  or delete the Episode.

  The protagonist must be
  a participant of the same Trip.

  The Episode date must fall
  within the Trip date interval.
end note


note right of SUBMITTED
  The Episode is visible to
  all Trip participants.

  The Episode becomes immutable.

  This state is transient:
  voting opens automatically
  after successful submission.
end note


note right of VOTING
  Only eligible participants
  may vote.

  Each eligible participant
  may vote at most once.

  Vote values must be
  integers from 1 to 5.

  The protagonist cannot vote.

  Submitted Votes cannot
  be modified or deleted.
end note


note right of COMPLETED
  All eligible participants
  have voted.

  No additional Votes
  are accepted.

  The final Episode score
  is the arithmetic mean
  of all valid Votes.

  The Episode contributes
  to the participant ranking.
end note

'General Contraint
note bottom
  Episode creation and lifecycle transitions occur only while the Trip is ACTIVE.
  Episodes remain available afterward for historical access.

  Backward transitions and
  skipped transitions are not allowed.

  SUBMITTED -> VOTING occurs
  automatically.
end note

@enduml
